WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:09.060
<v Grace Liu>Morning, everyone. Monday the 15th of June. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:17.070
<v Tomasz Nowak>We can hear you. Whose new car is that in the car park, then? Takes up most of the view.</v>

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:22.670
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one with a resale value of about half a sandwich.</v>

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:29.149
<v Marcus Hale>I'd swap it for somewhere cooler. The heating in the portakabin's having a laugh. It's June.</v>

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.750
<v Aisha Begum>You've got your own little tropical climate in there.</v>

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:41.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>Also, there's a birthday cake in the office. Just saying, before the early shift finishes it.</v>

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.840
<v Sarah Okafor>That's the most useful status update we've had all morning.</v>

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.920
<v Grace Liu>Right, before this becomes a cake allocation meeting. Finished stuff first, then the actual actions.</v>

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:59.880
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, so I already swapped the filter on the GT1 fuel valve yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.719
<v Priya Raman>Right, completed, not something still waiting on us.</v>

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:11.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. And I tested the line 1 TCU yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished as well.</v>

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.420
<v David Whitfield>Good. Two bits of yesterday's noise out of the way.</v>

00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:24.870
<v Marcus Hale>Same from me on the water booster. Already swapped the filter on the water booster yesterday.</v>

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.670
<v Grace Liu>Lovely. Those are completed updates, not new jobs.</v>

00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:36.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>I heard a slight rattle from the wrapper, by the way. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.689
<v David Whitfield>So you're not raising a repair off that?</v>

00:01:42.239 --> 00:01:47.489
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, no. Just saying what I heard. No job out of it at this point.</v>

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:54.700
<v Aisha Begum>Similar one from me: heard a slight rattle from the IM2, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.739
<v Grace Liu>Okay, both observations only.</v>

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:06.290
<v Priya Raman>And I'm still blocked on the site water. Can't get to the site water until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:11.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, there's no agreed window for that. It's not released work.</v>

00:02:12.919 --> 00:02:22.020
<v Grace Liu>Same position here: can't get to the Injection Moulding Line 1 until production gives us a window. That stays blocked, not a new action for today.</v>

00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:30.939
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, and we were going to replace the belt on the turbine one, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.659
<v Grace Liu>Right, that's off today's list as well. Onto what we are actually agreeing.</v>

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:46.530
<v Grace Liu>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the boiler feed pump. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:53.080
<v David Whitfield>Just so we're clear, it's the sign-off you're taking, rather than us bundling more work into that?</v>

00:02:54.319 --> 00:03:00.270
<v Grace Liu>Yes, the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the boiler feed pump. I'll take that, and it comes first.</v>

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:05.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood, Grace. That one's ahead of the rest for you.</v>

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:13.569
<v Grace Liu>Marcus, can you check the guarding on the Palletiser, tomorrow at 9:30? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:14.449 --> 00:03:19.000
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the Palletiser tomorrow at 9:30. Got it.</v>

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, talking over you there—guarding check, not a rebuild or anything?</v>

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.580
<v Marcus Hale>That's right, check the guarding. Tomorrow at 9:30, top priority.</v>

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:38.409
<v Grace Liu>And Marc, can you take vibration readings on the air compressor by the end of the week? Normal priority on that one.</v>

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:47.650
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll take vibration readings on the air compressor by the end of the week. Normal priority, separate from the guarding.</v>

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.159
<v David Whitfield>Useful distinction. Otherwise everything ends up with the same red flag beside it.</v>

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.479
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. The air compressor readings are normal priority; the Palletiser guarding is top priority.</v>

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:05.479
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on mine, I'll run a function test on the Line 3 Chiller after lunch.</v>

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.210
<v Aisha Begum>A function test, yeah? Not just a glance at the display.</v>

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.300
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, a function test on the Line 3 Chiller. That's what I'm taking on.</v>

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.529
<v Grace Liu>Thanks, Marc. After lunch, and top priority please.</v>

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.910
<v Marcus Hale>Agreed. After lunch, top priority.</v>

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:30.589
<v Grace Liu>Tomasz, can you run the monthly fire alarm test? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:39.699
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test. Understood, not an emergency, but it won't fall off my list.</v>

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:46.269
<v Priya Raman>The word 'monthly' always makes it sound ages away, doesn't it? Then suddenly it's here again.</v>

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:51.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. Months are getting shorter. Payslip doesn't seem to arrive any faster, mind.</v>

00:04:52.269 --> 00:04:57.170
<v Grace Liu>Um, I'll do the pre-use checks on the forklifts on Friday. That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:03.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Grace, you've got the pre-use checks on the forklifts on Friday.</v>

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:11.069
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll do those. Fairly important, but separate from the sign-off that needs doing first.</v>

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:19.579
<v Grace Liu>Saz, if you've got a spare minute, can you sort the training records for the new starters by end of day?</v>

00:05:22.009 --> 00:05:28.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters by end of day. I can take that.</v>

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.540
<v David Whitfield>A spare minute on a Monday. Rare engineering resource, that.</v>

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:39.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. But yes, by end of day. I've accepted it, before anyone thinks that was me wriggling out.</v>

00:05:41.189 --> 00:05:49.240
<v Grace Liu>Sarah, can you go to Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds to pick up the replacement parts for the cooling tower by the 28th? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:50.509 --> 00:05:58.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll go to Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds to pick up the replacement parts for the cooling tower by the 28th. Normal priority, understood.</v>

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.899
<v David Whitfield>That's the collection we're agreeing, not fitting the parts as well?</v>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:13.870
<v Grace Liu>Yes, just going to Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds to pick up the replacement parts for the cooling tower. No installation action being added.</v>

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:20.949
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll swap the filter on the air dryer on the 3rd. It's urgent.</v>

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:26.600
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, air dryer for that one? Not the filter you said you'd already done?</v>

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:36.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, the air dryer. I'll swap that filter on the 3rd; it's urgent. The GT1 fuel valve filter was yesterday and is already done.</v>

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:44.120
<v Grace Liu>Got you, Sarah. The air dryer is the new commitment, on the 3rd, urgent. Not reopening the finished one.</v>

00:06:45.519 --> 00:06:50.420
<v Aisha Begum>Good, because all the filters were starting to merge into one in my head.</v>

00:06:52.279 --> 00:06:56.129
<v Grace Liu>All clear on what's agreed, what's finished and what's still blocked?</v>

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.379
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, clear from me. No mystery extras hiding in the chat, hopefully.</v>

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:07.850
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing else from me. The cake was information only, before that gets an owner.</v>

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:14.800
<v Sarah Okafor>I think the cake's already got several owners. They're just not declaring themselves.</v>

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.360
<v Grace Liu>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
